Error [E0119]: there's no type called `View`
  --> tests/ui/task_detach_view_capture.jet:3:23
    |
  3 | fn peek(xs: [Int]) => View<Int> = xs[0..2]
    |                       ^^^^^^^^^
 Why: generic types must name a struct or enum you defined
 Fix: check the spelling, or define the type first

Error [E0119]: `View` isn't generic
  --> tests/ui/task_detach_view_capture.jet:3:23
    |
  3 | fn peek(xs: [Int]) => View<Int> = xs[0..2]
    |                       ^^^^^^^^^
 Why: only types declared with type parameters accept `<…>`
 Fix: use `View` without type arguments

Error [E2305]: a lambda cannot return a stored or borrowed view
  --> tests/ui/task_detach_view_capture.jet:7:22
    |
  7 |     t :: tasks.spawn(() => peek([1, 2, 3]))
    |                      ^^^^^^^^^^
 Why: a lambda value has no stable public owner slot for the returned view, and captured owners may move with the closure
 Fix: use a named function or method whose returned-view provenance can be inferred and published

Error [E1102]: this task returns a view that cannot be shared — it does not live long enough to cross into a task
  --> tests/ui/task_detach_view_capture.jet:7:22
    |
  7 |     t :: tasks.spawn(() => peek([1, 2, 3]))
    |                      ^^^^^^^^^^
 Why: a view is a borrow, not an owned value; tasks and channels move owned values between threads
 Fix: give the task plain owned data, or rebuild the value as an owned copy before spawning

Error [E1106]: can't detach task `t` — it captured a `view` borrow that may not live long enough
  --> tests/ui/task_detach_view_capture.jet:8:7
    |
  8 |     t.detach()
    |       ^^^^^^
 Why: a detached task runs unsupervised and may outlive the caller; a captured `view` would dangle
 Fix: pass an owned `copy`, or a `Shared<T>` handle, to the task instead of a `view`
